# Cloud-init is disabled by default on non-cloud VPS environments.
#
# Cloud-init tries to detect cloud metadata services (ConfigDrive, EC2, etc.)
# which don't exist on traditional VPS providers. This causes boot delays.
#
# To enable cloud-init on a cloud platform (AWS, CloudStack, etc.):
#   rm /etc/cloud-init.disabled
#
# Network configuration should be handled via DHCP or manual /etc/network/interfaces.
